From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:21:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] yblod-engine-vk: dual MMR within V3D's 4-thread
 register budget

- fel_chroma (the fused FEL chroma pass; with the bilinear EL upscale, the
  Pi 5's likely FEL route): the 64-bit-LUT MMR's term loop is kept rolled
  ([[dont_unroll]]). Unrolled, the scheduler hoisted every term's 64-bit
  product together: 64 registers, 2 threads. Now the dual-MMR variants
  compile to 32 registers and 4 threads (bilinear + CB1 contract: 1156
  instructions, 4 threads, no spills).
- fel_mmr_dual_horizontal, narrow variant: the two channels' MMR sums one
  after the other (mmr64_dual_pixel_sequential; exact integer sums, same
  results). 64 -> 62 registers: still 2 threads (the EL window loads).

Outputs identical (Annex B and nearest vs before; bilinear's fused path vs
its staged reference; CB1 == Vulkan; clean under the validation layer).
